    {
      "id": "ou7reuu",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Laws of Chemical Combination"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Dalton's Atomic Theory posits that all matter consists of indivisible particles known as atoms.",
        "Atoms combine in fixed integer ratios to form chemical compounds according to the Laws of Chemical Combination.",
        "Isotopes are atoms of the same element with identical atomic numbers but different mass numbers.",
        "Isobars share the same mass number despite having different atomic numbers, while isotones possess equal neutron counts.",
        "The Avogadro constant (6.022 × 10²³) defines the total number of particles present in one mole of a substance."
      ],
      "id": "jyyloyg"
    },
